From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:56:53 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] Review: a supervisor ended by a signal ends the job
 first; only ranks get a stack file

- A SIGTERM or SIGHUP to the supervisor left mpirun and the ranks running,
  and the tidy then unlinked the stack files the live ranks held open, so a
  later dump was lost; the parent also saw exit 143. The supervisor now kills
  the job's tree and waits for it (the kill ladder bounds it), tidies, and
  dies of the signal it was sent.
- Every Python process of the job got a stack file, a rank's own build
  subprocesses included, so after a kill a silent rank's empty file was lost
  among them. A process whose direct parent is an armed process (or a helper)
  of the same rank is a helper and gets none; a rank, a child of its launcher,
  is armed under any launcher. The rank is read from Open MPI's, PMIx's,
  MPICH/Hydra's, MVAPICH's or Slurm's variable, 'unknown' otherwise.
- ptest_jit_cache removes its fake build directories.

test_0063: a two-rank hang with one rank ignoring SIGUSR1 keeps that rank's
empty file and the other's stack, and the rank's python subprocess gets no
file; SIGTERM leaves no job process, the parent sees -15, and the job's
stack file was still there when it ended. Both fail before this change.

